tiffness                       three days as the fever could not be           and cause and effect\nCVS, RS & abdo – normal                 controlled by antipyretics. Therefore,             o Initially,\nAssessment                              blood and urine tests were ordered.                o However,\nViral infection                                                                            o Therefore,\nManagement\nKeep home from school\nRest and paracetamol three times\ndaily\nReview in 3 days if no improvement\n12/10/10\nSubjective\nAmina not well\nCough +, continuous headache,\nlethargic, loss of appetite\nDifficult to control temperature with\nParacetamol\nMother worried\nObjective\nFever 39.8 C\nNo rash or neck stiffness\nManagement\nPrescribe Brufen 200mg as required\nFBC & UFR were ordered\n\f\nReview in two days with results of\nreports\n14/10/10                                Regrettably, today Amina became            This paragraph explains the\nSubjective                              lethargic and listless. She vomited         current condition is detail\nBoth parents very concerned             twice last night and had been having       Supporting sentences expand\nReported Amina lethargic and listless   severe headaches. On examination,           the case notes into complete\nVomited twice last night and            she was severely febrile with a             sentences, note the use of\nheadaches worse                         temperature of 40.2 and a pulse rate        verbs, articles and\nObjective                               of 110 beats per minute. There was          conjunctions (and)\nFBC- WBC(18000) and left shift          macula-papular rash over the legs          Signal word shows empathy\nUrinary Function Report Normal          and neck stiffness was present. Blood           o Regrettably,\nTemperature 40.2C                       test showed leucocytosis with a shift           o On examination,\nPulse 110/min                           to the left..\nMacula-papular rash over legs\nNeck Stiffness+\n\nExample 2\n        Case Notes                                 Paragraphs                             Analysis\nMedical History                         Initially, she presented to me on          The topic sentence is begins\nThyroidism diagnosed Feb 07             21/2/10, complaining of inflamed,           with the first consultation\nHigh blood pressure June 09             sticky and weeping eyes. Both her          Supporting sentences\nHip replacement July 09                 eyes were reddish with watery               transform case notes into\nMedications – thyroxine 1mg daily,      discharge. However, her right eye           complete sentences\nAtacand 4mg daily, Fosamax 10mg         was worse than the left eye.               Includes both medical history\ndaily                                   Therefore, she was prescribed               and initial consultation\nNo known allergies                      chlorisig drops 4 hourly. In terms of      Signal words express a time\n21.02.10                                her medical history, she has had            line, contrast and cause and\nSubjective                              thyroidism for 3 years, high blood          effect.\nComplains of inflamed, sticky and       pressure for 1 year and a hip                   o Initially,\nweeping eyes.                           replacement was done in 2005. Her               o However,\nObjective                               current medications are Thyroxin 1              o Therefore,\nBP 135 /75 P 74                         mg, Atacand 4 mg and Fosamax 10                 o In terms of...\nBoth eyes – red, watery discharge       mg daily. She has no known allergies.           o ..current\nright eye worse than left\n\n\n03.03.10                              On review 2 weeks later, she had             Topic sentence is introduced\nSubjective                            made no improvement. In              