\nRe: Mr. Jing Zu, 72, married, retired school teacher\n\nThank you for seeing Mr. Zu who is suffering from deteriorating\ncoronary heart disease.\n\nMr. Zu’s medical history includes hypertension for 18 years and        Medical history\nischemic heart disease for 10 years. He had an acute myocardial\ninfarction in 1999 and has had chronic cardiac failure (CCF) for\nfive years. His current medications are as follows: Lasix 80 mg\nand Enalapril 10 mg daily, slow-released potassium twice daily,\nnifedipine 10 mg three times a day and Anginine when necessary.\n\nThe patient initially presented on 3 January 2007 with exertion-       Recent medical history of disease being referred for. (in this case\ninduced angina, which improved with rest and Anginine. In              over a number of visits – starting with first of this series)\naddition, he had the typical manifestations of chronic heart failure\nand postural BP drop. Thus, he was observed for stable CCF and\nangina.\n\nMr. Zu also experienced an episode of exacerbation of his CCF          The next phase – could go with previous?\non 15th of January and consequently was treated with increased\ndose of the Lasix at 80 mg daily.\n\nOn review today, although his dyspnea has responded to Lasix,          On day of referral.\nthe patient reported a 10-minute- attack of angina (OR a 10-\nminute angina attack) yesterday. The ECG revealed suspicious\nanterolateral ischemic changes.\n\nGiven Mr. Zu’s history of acute myocardial infarction and the          Request for help + offer of further information.\natypical ischemic changes of his ECG, I would appreciate your\nfurther assessment and management regarding his angina.\nPlease do not hesitate to contact me if you require further\ninformation.\n\nYours sincerely\n\nXXXXXXX\n\n(words 205)\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\n\n\f\nA to Z of Phrasal Verbs and Useful Vocabulary\n Letter           