als", "x": 0.8479907189542484, "width": 0.06227529411764707, "confidence": 1}]}, {"text": "correctly?", "x": 0.7202777777777778, "y": 0.5667797979797979, "width": 0.08029411764705881, "height": 0.01546363636363639, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "correctly?", "x": 0.7202777777777778, "width": 0.08029411764705881, "confidence": 1}]}, {"text": "Are there a lot of spelling", "x": 0.7202777777777778, "y": 0.5819313131313131, "width": 0.20887999999999993, "height": 0.01546363636363639, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "Are", "x": 0.7202777777777778, "width": 0.02819764705882352, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "there", "x": 0.7539766013071895, "width": 0.0435152941176471, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "a", "x": 0.8033554248366014, "width": 0.009898823529411701, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "lot", "x": 0.818623660130719, "width": 0.02058823529411759, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "of", "x": 0.8452401307189543, "width": 0.015597647058823485, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "spelling", "x": 0.8663883660130719, "width": 0.06276941176470575, "confidence": 1}]}, {"text": "errors?", "x": 0.7202777777777778, "y": 0.5973858585858586, "width": 0.058371764705882366, "height": 0.01546363636363639, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "errors?", "x": 0.7202777777777778, "width": 0.058371764705882366, "confidence": 1}]}]}]}}}, {"number": 100, "text": "Writing Sub-Test Overview\nThe writing sub-test is usually a letter of referral but it may also be a letter requesting or giving advice. Candidates\nare given patient case notes and sometimes other information along with task instructions. The test procedure is as\nfollows:\n\n   1. 5 minutes reading time, during which you can not take notes or underline any details\n   2. 40 minutes to read the task and write your letter in a booklet provided. You can use pen or pencil.\n\nYou can expect the stimulus material to be between 2 & 3 pages long and include detailed social & medical\nhistory. Most tasks will require you to identify the important aspects of the history and summarize this into letter\nformat. Unlike other professions, most tasks are referral letters between doctors. The important point is to always\nread the task question carefully and respond appropriately.\n\n   Handy Hint\nDo not just summarize the medical history. Always consider what the referred to person needs to know and what\nthey will do with information. The social factors are sometimes very significant, hence the need for ongoing care,\nand are included to make the task more complex and challenging for the candidate.\n\n                                                  Task Types\n             Letter Type                   Chief Complaint & Purpose of           Complicating factors in case notes\n                                                    Writing\n      Referral from GP to Duty             Meningococcal meningitis                 Complex social factors\n       Registrar in Hospital                                                           including language barrier\n                                                                                      Detailed and long medical\n                                                                                       history\n\n      Referral from GP to Pyschiatrist       Schizophrenia                          Complex social factors\n                                                                                      Medical history\n\n      Referral from GP to Admitting          Peritonitis                            Significant medical history\n       Doctor Emergency Department                                                    Urgent case\n                                                                                      Socio-economic situation of\n                                                                                       patient\n\n      Referral from GP to                    Fertility problem                      Confidentiality\n       Gynaecologist at a Fertility                                                   Conflicting views of husband\n       Clinic                                                                          and wife and GP\n                                                                                      Detailed medical history\n\n      Referral from GP to Consultant         Antenatal care                         Only one very detailed\n       Obstetrician at a Mother's                                                      consultation\n       Hospital\n\n      Referral from GP to                    Diabetes                               Complex social history\n       Endocrinologist                                                                Long medical history\n\n      Referral from GP                       Subdural haematoma                     Urgent situation\n       to Neurosurgeon                                                                Detailed social and medical\n                                                                                       history\n\n      Referral from GP to Pyschiatrist       Anorexia Nervosa                       Complex social history", "extraction": "text", "display": {"version": 2, "text": "Writing Sub-Test Overview\n\nThe writing sub-test is usually a letter of referral but it may also be a letter requesting or giving advice. Candidates\nare given patient case notes and sometimes other information along with task instructions. The test procedure is as\nfollows:\n\n1. 5 minutes reading time, during which you can not take notes or underline any details\n2. 40 minutes to read the task and write your letter in a booklet provided. You can use pen or pencil.\n\nYou can expect the stimulus material to be between 2 & 3 pages long and include detailed social & medical\nhistory. Most tasks will require you to identify the important aspects of the history and summarize this into letter\nformat. Unlike other professions, most tasks are referral letters between doctors. The important point is to always\nread the task question carefully and respond appropriately.\n\nHandy Hint\nDo not just summarize the medical history. Always consider what the referred to person needs to know and what\nthey will do with information. The social factors are sometimes very significant, hence the need for ongoing care,\nand are included to make the task more complex and challenging for the candidate.\n\nLetter Type\n\n\n\nReferral from GP to Duty\nRegistrar in Hospital\n\nTask Types\nChief Complaint & Purpose of\nWriting\n Meningococcal meningitis\n\nComplicating factors in case notes\n\n\n\n\n\nComplex social factors\nincluding language barrier\nDetailed and long medical\nhistory\n\n\n\nReferral from GP to Pyschiatrist\n\n\n\nSchizophrenia\n\n\n\n\nComplex social factors\nMedical history\n\n\n\nReferral from GP to Admitting\nDoctor Emergency Department\n\n\n\nPeritonitis\n\n\n\n\n\nSignificant medical history\nUrgent case\nSocio-economic situation of\npatient\n\n\n\nReferral from GP to\nGynaecologist at a Fertility\nClinic\n\n\n\nFertility problem\n\n\n\n\nConfidentiality\nConflicting views of husband\nand wife and GP\nDetailed medical history\n\n\n\n\n\nReferral from GP to Consultant\nObstetrician at a Mother's\nHospital\n\n\n\nAntenatal care\n\n\n\nOnly one very detailed\nconsultation\n\n\n\nReferral from GP to\nEndocrinologist\n\n\n\nDiabetes\n\n\n\n\nComplex social history\nLong medical history\n\n\n\nReferral from GP\nto Neurosurgeon\n\n\n\nSubdural haematoma\n\n\n\n\nUrgent situation\nDetailed social and medical\nhistory\n\n\n\nReferral from GP to Pyschiatrist\n\n\n\nAnorexia Nervosa\n\n\n\nComplex social history", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 612.0, "height": 792.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Writing Sub-Test Overview", "lines": [{"text": "Writing Sub-Test Overview", "x": 0.25968954248366016, "y": 0.017146969696969695, "width": 0.4949743790849673, "height": 0.0305590909