\nformal writing. Can and will are\nconsidered less polite than could and\nwould.\n\nExplanation: These sentences are\nacceptable in written English, but can\nsound quite direct.\n\n•\n\nIt would be greatly appreciated\nif you could examine, diagnose\nand treat the patient as you feel\nappropriate. (passive and most\npolite)\nI hope you can arrange\nsomeone to help this family and\nprovide proper medical\nsupport.\n\nExplanation: These sentences are the\nmost suitable for concluding requests in\nformal letters .\n\nConditional Sentences: These sentences are also frequently used in the conclusion of a referral letter and the rules are as\nfollows:\n\nUse a comma when the if clause is at the beginning of the\nsentence.\n\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n\nDon’t use a comma when the if clause is at the end of the\nsentence.\n\nIf you could take over her on going care,it would be\ngreatly appreciated .\nIf you have any further questions regarding this\npatient, please don’t hesitate to call me.\n\n•\n\nIf you require any more information, please don't\nhesitate to contact me.(active)\nIf any more information is required, please don't\nhesitate to contact me.(passive)\n\n•\n\nShould you have any further queries, please don't\nhesitate to contact me .\n\n•\n\n•\n\n•\n\nIt would be greatly appreciated if you could take\nover her ongoing care.\nPlease don’t hesitate to call me if you have any\nfurther questions regarding this patient.\n\nPlease don't hesitate to contact me if you require any\nmore information.(active)\nPlease don't hesitate to contact me if any more\ninformation is required.(passive)\n\nPlease don't hesitate to contact me should you have\nany further queries .\n\nNote: Sometimes if is omitted from a conditional sentence. In\nfull the sentence means:\nIf you should have any further questions regarding this\npatient, please don’t hesitate to call me.\n\nCloser and signature\nLeave a space between the last line of the conclusion and the closer. The closer should be followed by a comma. Then write\nyour signature below the closer, and if you have time, print your name below your signature.\n\nSample Conclusions\n\nCase Notes\n\nConclusion\n\nWriting Task\nIn order to maintain a good health\nMr O’Riley has requested advice on low condition, Mr. O’Riley has requested\nfat dietary guidelines and healthy simple advice on low fat dietary guidelines and\nrecipes. Write a letter to the Community healthy simple recipes. It would be\nInformation Section of the Heart\ngreatly appreciated if you could send the\nFoundation, Gregory Terrace, Brisbane above mentioned information to Mr.\non the patient's behalf. Use the relevant O’Riley at his home address, 9476 Old\ncase notes to explain Mr O’Riley’s\nDam Road, Goondiwindi, QLD, 4390.\nsituation and the information he needs.\nInclude Medical History, Body Mass\nYours sincerely,\nIndex and lifestyle. Information should\nbe sent to his home address.\nLee Wong Charge Nurse\n\nAnalysis\n\n•\n\n•\n•\n\n•\n\nUses information from the\nwriting task to formulate\nconclusion\nContains a polite request\nMaintains polite tone through\nthe use of modal verbs would\nand could\nContains information specific\nto the task", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 612.0, "height": 792.0, "blocks": [{"text": "•", "lines": [{"text": "•", "x": 0.6820751633986928, "y": 0.04933106060606061, "width": 0.0074862745098038894, "height": 0.015405303030303031, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "•", "x": 0.6820751633986928, "width": 0.0074862745098038894, "confidence": 1}]}]}, {"text": "Explanation: These sentences are fine\nin spoken English, but not suitable for\nformal writing. Can and will are\nconsidered less polite than could and\nwould.", "lines": [{"text": "Explanation: These sentences are fine", "x": 0.1012156862745098, "y": 0.10791116161616161, "width": 0.2537834640522875, "height": 0.013921363636363645, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "Explanation:", "x": 0.1012156862745098, "width": 0.09064901960784313, "confide