necessary to state them.\n\n\n   •   As per the doctor’s order, we were          •    As per the doctor’s order, daily home\n       organized daily home visits.                     visits were organized. (passive)\n\n                                                   •    As per the doctor’s order, we\n                                                        organised daily home visits. (active)\n\n                                               Both sentences are grammatically correct but the first\n                                               example is preferred because it focuses attention on\n                                               the procedure.\n\n\n   •   On 9.7.06 he was presented to me for        •    On 9.7.06, he presented to me for his\n       his regular check up.                            regular check up. (active)\n\n                                               Active voice is preferred here as the patient is the\n                                               subject and most likely presented himself.\n\n\n   •   On the subsequent visit the treatment       •    On the subsequent visit, the treatment\n       options was discussed.                           options were discussed.\n\n                                               Because the noun is plural the plural verb “were” is\n                                               required.\n\n\n\n   •   She had done colonoscopy 3 years            •    A colonoscopy was done 3 years ago.\n       ago.\n                                                   •    She had a colonoscopy done 3 years\n                                                        ago.\n\n                                               In these sentences it is unimportant who performed the", "extraction": "text", "display": {"version": 2, "text": "aspirin in the evening.\n\nthe evening.\n\nPlease review the list of common mistakes below.\nIncorrect\n\n•\n\nShe was performed a colostomy\naccompanied with a partial bowel\nresectio