th": 0.029082352941176427, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "of", "x": 0.6259428571428571, "width": 0.016800000000000065, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "the", "x": 0.6477848739495798, "width": 0.024584873949579807, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "sentence.", "x": 0.6773714285714286, "width": 0.07444033613445374, "confidence": 1}]}]}]}}}, {"number": 206, "text": "   It would be greatly appreciated if you could take over her antenatal\n                      care.\n\n                     Please don’t hesitate to call me if you have any further questions\n                      regarding this patient.\n\n4. Complex sentences:\n\n           o Use a comma if the dependent clause is at the beginning of the sentence.\n\n                     In case of irritation, redness or swelling, please consult your doctor.\n\n                     When the results become available, I will forward them to you.\n\n                     Because of her deteriorating condition, the patient was admitted to\n                      hospital.\n\n           o Don’t use a comma if the dependent clause is at the end of the sentence.\n\n                     Please consult your doctor in case of irritation, redness or swelling.\n\n                     I will forward the results to you when they become available.\n\n                     The patient was admitted to hospital because of her deteriorating\n                      condition.\n\n5. Comma Splices: A comma splice is two sentences joined together with a comma, but no\nconjunction. This is an error as the information must be either joined with a coordinating\nconjunction such as and/but/or or a new sentence must be started.\n\n           o He does not have any dental experience, he is worried about the pain.\n             (incorrect)\n\n           o He does not have any dental experience and he is worried about the pain.\n             (correct)\n\n           o He does not have any dental experience. Therefore, he is worried about the\n             pain.(