                       situations. (adjective form)\n\n\n                                  a few/few & a little/little\nFew and a few is used with plural nouns, and little and a little is used with uncountable\nnouns. Little and few have negative connotations and are similar in many to not much/ not\nmany. A little and a few have positive connotations and are similar in meaning to some.\nMixing up these words therefore will completely change the meaning of the sentence.\n\n                  Incorrect                                           Correct\n\n   •   The patient has reduced speech output        •   The patient has reduced speech output\n       and a little eye contact.                        and little eye contact.(negative\n                                                        connotation required here)\n   •   There are few ways to help identify\n       the possibility of threadworms such as       •   There are a few ways to help identify\n       checking the anus of your children at            the possibility of threadworms such as\n       night and frequent scratching.                   checking the anus of your children at\n                                                        night and frequent scratching.(positive\n                                                        connotation required)\n\n\n                                         during/while\nDuring is followed by a noun\n\n   •   During hospitalisation, the patient made a full recovery.\n\n   •   The patient had many visitors during his stay in hospital.", "extraction": "text", "display": {"version": 2, "text": "(adjective)\n\nConfident Vs Confidence\n\nConfident is an adjective\n\n•\n\nThe patient is not confident in her ability as a mother.\n\nConfidence is a noun\n\n•\n\nThe patient lacks confidence in her ability as a mother.\n\nIncorrect\n\nCorrect\n\n•\n\nThe patient has not confident social\nsituations.\n\n•\n\nThe patient has no confidence in\nsocial situations. (noun form)\n\n•\n\nThe patient is not confidence in social\nsituations.\n\n•\n\nThe patient is not confident in social\nsituations. (adjective form)\n\na few/few & a little/little\nFew and a few is used with plural nouns, and little and a little is used with uncountable\nnouns. Little and few have negative connotations and are similar in many to not much/ not\nmany. A little and a few have positive connotations and are similar in meaning to some.\nMixing up these words therefore will completely change the meaning of the sentence.\n\nIncorrect\n\nCorrect\n\n•\n\nThe patient has reduced speech output\nand a little eye contact.\n\n•\n\nThere are few ways to help identify\nthe possibility of threadworms such as\nchecking the anus of your children at\nnight and frequent scratching.\n\n•\n\nThe patient has reduced speech output\nand little eye contact.(negative\nconnotation required here)\n\n•\n\nThere are a few ways to help identify\nthe possibility of threadworms such as\nchecking the anus of your children at\nnight and frequent scratching.(positive\nconnotation required)\n\nduring/while\n\nDuring is followed by a noun\n\n•\n\nDuring hospitalisation, the patient made a full recovery.\n\n•\n\nThe patient had many visitors during his stay in hospital.", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 595.0, "height": 842.0, "blocks": [{"text": "(adjective)", "lines": [{"text": "(adjective)", "x": 0.5608403361344537, "y": 0.10725415676959621, "width": 0.08617815126050422, "height": 0.015776722090261274, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "(adjective)", "x": 0.5608403361344537, "width": 0.08617815126050422, "confidence": 1}]}]}, {"text": "Confident Vs Confidence", "lines": [{"text": "Confident Vs Confidence", "x": 0.39260504201680674, "y": 0.16105463182897864, "width": 0.21567731092436976, "height": 0.015776722090261274, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "Confident", "x": 0.39260504201680674, "width": 0.08613781512605038, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "Vs", "x": 0.4836235294117647, "width": 0.0221243697