     C+\n     Estimated Score           320/500\n     Advice                     1. Develop the purpose of the document clearly in the\n                                   introduction.\n                                2. Always read and select case notes carefully.\n                                3. Refer to the patient appropriately in the letter.\n                                4. Avoid basic grammar errors.\n                                5. Punctuate the content appropriately.\n                                6. Pay attention to capitalization.\n                                7. Improve choice of words.\n                                8. Improve the structure of sentences.\n                                9. Avoid using outdated/informal/academic connectors.\n\n\n\nhttps://edubenchmark.com", "extraction": "text"}, {"number": 309, "text": "Ticket Id: 151175\n\n                             10. For urgent referrals, give priority to the most recent symptoms\n                                 and needs.\n                             11. Improve paragraphing.\n                             12. Try to finish the letter in 200 words by writing information in\n                                 brief wherever possible. Watch this video on word length:\n                                 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AyaIEjPv6Ag\n                             13. Use appropriate salutations in the letter.\n                             14. Always proofread the letter after finishing it.\n\n    Free Resources           Facebook Group       OET Blog       Free OET Course\n    Bulk Packages            Regular 20 Regular 30 Regular 50\n\n                             Urgent 20     Urgent 30     Urgent 50\n\n                             For more info, contact info@edubenchmark.com\n    Buy Direct By Clicking   Regular 8 Letter Package    (New case notes on repurchase)\n    the Hyperlinks\n                             Urgent 4 Letter Package     (New case notes on repurchase)\n\n                             OET Reading Comprehensive Course – 20 Reading Tests\n\n                             OET Intensive Listening Tests – 15 Listening Tests\n\n                             OET Essentials Course – 20 Full OET Tests (Writing correction not\n                             included)\n\n                             OET Pro Course – OET Essentials + 4 Urgent Letter Corrections\n\n                             OET Speaking Mock Test\n\n    Also Preparing IELTS?    IELTS Writing Correction Service\n    Try IELTS Writing\n    Correction service\n\n\n\n\nhttps://edubenchmark.com", "extraction": "text"}, {"number": 310, "text": "Ticket Id: 151408\n\n24/12/2021\n\nMr. Edward Collins\nDirector\nMary Curie Physical and Mental Health Rehabilitation Center\n\nRe: Mr. Peter Berry, 30 years old\nDear Mr. Collins,\n\nI am writing to refer Mr. Peter Berry, who has been admitted in our our hospital for six months with head    Commented [ESL1]: transfer\ntrauma following a road traffic accident, for your kind care.                                                Commented [ESL2]: is recovering from a\n                                                                                                             Commented [ESL3]: further rehabilitation\nRegarding his history, Mr. Berry is a single accountant who smokes nine cigarettes per day and consumes\n                                                                                                             Commented [ESL4]: *(Sequence the information\nalcohol moderately. It’s worth mentioning that he has acquired over speeding fines frequently. Please        logically based on importance.)\nnote, his mother Mrs. Amelia Andy is his next of kin.                                                        Commented [ESL5]: It is\n                                                                                                             (Use of contractions affects the style.)\nInitially, on 26/06/2021, Mr. Berry was brou