 be highly appreciated.                                         Comment [OET2]: treated for\n\nInitially, on 17/12/2021, Ms. Grace presented to emergency in an aggressive condition. She had been           Comment [OET3]: On\nhallucinating, and refusing to eat or drink or take her medications. As a result, she was admitted, and\nreceived diazepam and halopridol IM. Over the next following days, Ms. Grace has been improving;              Comment [OET4]: few\ntherefore, she was commenced on risperidone, procyclidine and lorazepam. This treatment started               Comment [OET5]: was not improving\ngiving results in terms of all her symptoms.\n\nOn today’s review, Ms. Grace reported sleeping and eating well. In addition, she denied any delusions or      Comment [OET6]: was\nhallucinations. Her discharge medications include procyclidine 5 mg twice per day, and an IM injection of     Comment [OET7]: fortnightly\nclopixol 200 mg on 09/01/2022. Please note that Mrs. Grace is divorced, and has limited social support.       Comment [OET8]: C\nThis is her seventh hospital admission since her diagnosis with schizophrenia back in 2015.\n                                                                                                              Comment [OET9]: ; the next one is due\n                                                                                                              Comment [OET10]: already known to\nBased on the above, Mrs. Grace would need rehabilitation, psychosocial skills training, and ensuring her      the addressee\ncompliance with treatment. Should you have any queries, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n                                                                                                              Comment [OET11]: encouragement to\n                                                                                                              comply\nYours sincerely,\nDoctor\n\n\n\n                                             