-", "x": 0.5300699346405229, "width": 0.005876470588235229, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "200", "x": 0.5405452287581699, "width": 0.026809411764705946, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "words.", "x": 0.5720169934640523, "width": 0.048388235294117586, "confidence": 1}]}]}]}}}, {"number": 403, "text": "Physiotherapy Letter\n\n\n    OCCUPATIONAL ENGLISH TEST\n    WRITING SUB-TEST:                       PHYSIOTHERAPY\n    TIME ALLOWED:                           READING TIME:                   5 MINUTES\n                                            WRITING TIME:                   40 MINUTES\n    Read the case notes and complete the writing task which follows.\n\n\n\n\n    Notes:\n\n    You are a physiotherapist in private practice. Max Wolff has been referred to you by his GP, Dr William Stacey, for review\n    and a treatment plan after presenting with chronic back pain.\n\n    Physiotherapy Notes – from initial consultation 1 May 2010\n\n    Personal Details:\n    Name:            Max Wolff (Mr)\n    Age:             35\n    Profession:      Full-time musician: orchestral double bass player\n                     Lives with spouse, also a musician\n                     No dependants\n\n    Family/Patient History:\n                     Father (70) has mild osteoarthritis; mother (67) healthy\n                     Younger brother & sister healthy\n                     Tonsillectomy/adenoidectomy (1979)\n                     Myopic (corrective lenses since age 14)\n                     Non-smoker; ‘social’ drinker (8-10 units/week)\n                     Mild idiopathic scoliosis (<20º, untreated) since teenage years: slouching at desk while\n                     studying at school & music college\n                     Minor, ongoing postural problems from music college to present: daily work routine\n                     (practising, attending rehearsals & performing with orchestra); pain not a problem\n                     until recently\n                     Little formal exercise (no sports, no gym); busy schedule, with frequent evening work\n\n    Subjective:      Pt complains of ongoing upper back pain – feels stiff, ‘frozen’, ‘locked’ between shoulders;\n                     also dull pain in lumbar region\n                     Agg: prolonged performance on instrument (>2 hrs); ease: rest\n\n                     Symptoms developing over last 6-10 months; pt too busy at work to attend GP; has been using non-\n                     prescription analgesics lately for relief (to help with sleep, esp. after evening performances)\n\n\n    TURN OVER                                                                                                               2", "extraction": "text", "display": {"version": 2, "text": "Physiotherapy Letter\n\nOCCUPATIONAL ENGLISH TEST\n\nWRITING SUB-TEST:\n\nPHYSIOTHERAPY\n\nTIME ALLOWED:\n\nREADING TIME:\n\n5 MINUTES\n\nWRITING TIME:\n\n40 MINUTES\n\nRead the case notes and complete the writing task which follows.\n\nNotes:\n\nYou are a physiotherapist in private practice. Max Wolff has been referred to you by his GP, Dr William Stacey, for review\nand a treatment plan after presenting with chronic back pain.\n\nPhysiotherapy Notes – from initial consultation 1 May 2010\n\nPersonal Details:\n\nName:\nAge:\nProfession:\n\nMax Wolff (Mr)\n35\nFull-time musician: orchestral double bass player\nLives with spouse, also a musician\nNo dependants\n\nFamily/Patient History:\n\nFather (70) has mild osteoarthritis; mother (67) healthy\nYounger brother & sister healthy\n\nTonsillectomy/adenoidectomy (1979)\nMyopic (corrective lenses since age 14)\n\nNon-smoker; ‘social’ drinker (8-10 units/week)\n\nMild idiopathic scoliosis (<20º, untreated) since teenage years: slouching at desk while\nstudying at school & music college\n\nMinor, ongoing postural problems from music college to present: daily work routine\n(practising, attending rehearsals & performing with orchestra); pain not a problem\nuntil recently\n\nLittle formal exercise (no sports, no gym); busy schedule, with frequent evening work\n\nSubjective:\n\nPt complains of ongoing upper back pain – feels stiff, ‘frozen’, ‘locked’ between shoulders;\nalso dull pain in lumbar region\n\nAgg: prolonged performance on instrument (>2 hrs); ease: rest\n\nSymptoms developing over last 6-10 months; pt too busy at work to attend GP; has been using non-\nprescription analgesics lately for relief (to help with sleep, esp. after evening performances)\n\nTURN OVER\n\n2", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 595.276, "height": 841.89, "blocks": [{"text": "Physiotherapy Letter", "lines": [{"text": "Physiotherapy Letter", "x": 0.052778879040982676, "y": 0.01220111891102163, "width": 0.3929471371263078, "height": 0.044865718799368084, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "Physiotherapy", "x": 0.052778879040982676, "width": 0.27083907296783344, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "Letter", "x": 0.3342953520719801, "width": 0.11143066409531041, "confidence": 1}]}]}, {"text": "OCCUPATIONAL ENGLISH TEST", "lines": [{"text": "OCCUPATIONAL ENGLISH TEST", "x": 0.14285709486019932, "y": 0.12121203482640251, "width": 0.6205256049294782, "height": 0.03398068631293875, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "OCCUPATIONAL", "x": 0.14285709486019932, "width": 0.31810454310269526, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "ENGLISH", "x": 0.47216988422177275, "width": 0.1784449566251621, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "TEST", "x": 0.6618230871058132, "width": 0.10155961268386433, "confidence": 1}]}]}, {"text": "WRITING SUB-TEST:", "lines": [{"text": "WRITING SUB-TEST:", "x": 0.14285709486019932, "y": 0.165348323415173, "width": 0.23123391502429128, "height": 0.019822067015880955, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "WRITING", "x": 0.14285709486019932, "width": 0.10270529972651343, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "SUB-TEST:", "x": 0.25210053823772505, "width": 0.12199047164676553, "confidence": 1}]}]}, {"text": "PHYSIOTHERAPY", "lines": [{"text": "PHYSIOTHERAPY", "x": 0.406593580120818, "y": 0.16534832341