admitted to hospital for observation. (correct\n   as 2 past events need to be distinguished)\n\n   Handy Hint 2\nPast perfect is often used with the word previous instead of ago to demonstrate that you are referring to\na time before a particular date in the past, not the date you are writing the letter. See below for examples.\n                            Incorrect                                                       Correct\n\n    She presented to me on 03/07/2015 for a regular check up\n    because she experienced several episode of heart ﬂutter\n    over the past few weeks.\n                                                                        She presented to me on 03/07/2015 for a regular\n    Past perfect tense is necessary here (had experienced) to\n                                                                        check up because she had experienced several\n    differentiate what happened prior to the check up, which is\n                                                                        episodes of heart ﬂutter over the previous few\n    also in the past.\n                                                                        weeks.\n    As your meaning is prior to 03/07/105and not the day of\n    writing the letter, you should use the word previous instead of\n    past.", "extraction": "text"}, {"number": 687, "text": "On review two weeks later, the frequency of headache\n     decreased.                                                       On review two weeks later, the frequency of\n          Use past perfect to indicate that frequency of headache     headache had decreased.\n          had decreased prior to the consultation.\n\n\n\n     A review on 25/04/15 showed the patient’s general health\n     improved and her blood pressure dropped to 140/85 and            A review on 25/04/15 showed the patient’s general\n     she lost 4 kg.                                                   health had improved and her blood pressure had\n     Pas