ir case.                                               not unusual in their case.\n     I have already explained the couple the basic advice                 I told them that unsuccessful conception was not\n     regarding conception.                                                unusual in their case.\n                                                                          I have already explained to the couple basic advice\n Explanation: The word explain cannot be followed by a\n pronoun or noun without the preposition to whereas tell can.             regarding conception.\n                                                                          I have already told the couple basic advice regarding\n                                                                          conception.\n\n\n\n\n                                                         Advise Vs Advice\nAdvise is a verb\n\n    We advise patients on how to take their medication.\n\nAdvice is a noun\n\n    We give advice or provide advice to patients on how to take their medication.\n\nNote 1: The noun advice is uncountable so it can not be used in plural form. i.e. advices is incorrect as is an advice.\n\n    I gave some advice to the patient regarding her medication.\n\nNote 2: The pronunciation is different: advise advice\n\n                              Incorrect                                                            Correct\n     It would be greatly appreciated if you could make a                  It would be greatly appreciated if you could make a visit\n     visit to this family and advice his parents regarding                to this family and advise his parents regarding the\n     the recommended vaccines for both children.                          recommended vaccines for both children. (verb)\n     I am writing to refer this patient to you for an advice              I am writing to refer this patient to you for advice\n     regarding the management of his bilateral inguinal                   regarding the management of his bilateral inguinal\n     hernia.                                                              hernia(noun)\n     I gave an advice to the patient regarding her medication.            I gave some advice to the patient regarding her\n     I gave advices to the patient regarding her medication.              medication.(noun)\n     Please advice the patient on how and when to take their              I gave advice to the patient regarding her medication.\n     medication.                                                          (noun)\n                                                                          Please advise the patient on how and when to take their\n                                                                          medication. (verb)\n\n\n\n\n                                                               Request\nRequest can be both a verb and noun.\nRequest as a verb\n\n    The patient requested painkillers. (verb form)\n\nRequest as a noun\n\n    The patient made a request for painkillers. (noun form: request+for)", "extraction": "text", "display": {"version": 2, "text": "Explain Vs Tell\n\nExplain and tell also have different rules which cause confusion\n\nIncorrect\n\nCorrect\n\nI explained them that unsuccessful conception was not\n\nI explained to them that unsuccessful conception was\n\nunusual in their case.\n\nnot unusual in their case.\n\nI have already explained the couple the basic advice\n\nI told them that unsuccessful conception was not\n\nregarding conception.\n\nunusual in their case.\n\nExplanation: The word explain cannot be followed by a\npronoun or noun without the preposition to whereas tell can.\n\nI have already explained to the couple basic advice\n\nregarding conception.\n\nI have already told the couple basic advice regarding\n\nconception.\n\nAdvise Vs Advice\n\nAdvise is a verb\n\nWe advise patients on how to take their medication.\n\nAdvice is a noun\n\nWe give advice or provide advice to patients on how to take their medication.\n\nNote 1: The noun advice is uncountable so it can not be used in plural form. i.e. advices is incorrect as is an advice.\n\nI gave some advice to the patient regarding her medication.\n\nNote 2: The pronunciation is different: advise advice\n\nIncorrect\n\nCorrect\n\nIt would be greatly appreciated if you could make a\n\nIt would be greatly appreciated if you could make a visit\n\nvisit to this family and advice his parents regarding\n\nto this family and advise his parents regarding the\n\nthe recommended vaccines for both children.\n\nrecommended vaccines for both children. (verb)\n\nI am writing to refer this patient to you for an advice\n\nI am writing to refer this patient to you for advice\n\nregarding the management of his bilateral inguinal\n\nregarding the management of his bilateral inguinal\n\nhernia.\n\nhernia(noun)\n\nI gave an advice to the patient regarding her medication.\n\nI gave some advice to the patient regarding her\n\nI gave advices to the patient regarding her medication.\n\nmedication.(noun)\n\nPlease advice the patient on how and when to take their\n\nI gave advice to the patient regarding her medication.\n\nmedication.\n\n(noun)\n\nPlease advise the patient on how and when to take their\n\nmedication. (verb)\n\nRequest\n\nRequest can be both a verb and noun.\nRequest as a verb\n\nThe patient requested painkillers. (verb form)\n\nRequest as a noun\n\nThe patient made a request for painkillers. (noun form: request+for)", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 612.0, "height": 792.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Explain Vs Tell", "lines": [{"text": "Explain Vs Tell", "x": 0.4352728758169935, "y": 0.016578575757575757, "width": 0.1291563235294118, "height": 0.017803449494949497, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "Explain", "x": 0.4352728758169935, "width": 0.06410832352941173, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "Vs", "x": 0.5042781307189543, "width": 0.022976851307189506, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "Tell", "x": 