240196078514, "confidence": 1}]}]}]}}}, {"number": 725, "text": "Grammar & Vocabular y Clinic\n\n\n\n\nPhysical Decription\n\n\n                                                                                                            Return to: Topic 5 \n\n                                 Common Mistakes Regarding Physical Description\n\n                           Incorrect                                                           Correct\n\n Advice was given to reduce her weight.\n                                                                        Advice was given to reduce weight.\n After the verb reduce it is not necessary to follow with a             The patient was advised to reduce weight.\n pronoun. So you is not required. Simply say:\n                                                                        A reduction of weight was advised.\n I advised him to reduce weight, or, you need to reduce weight.\n\n\n In addition, she had lost her weight.\n                                                                        In addition, she had lost weight.\n After the verb lose it is not correct to follow with a pronoun.        In addition, she has lost a further 11 kg of weight over\n                                                                        the past 2 months.\n                                                                        In addition, the patient’s weight has signiﬁcantly\n                                                                        reduced from 61 kg to 50 kg over the past 2 months.\n\n\n He is now obese with a 99kilos weight and a 170cm height.\n                                                                        He is now obese with a weight of 99 kg and a height\n The use of the correct verb & noun form and associated                 of 170cm. (noun form)\n grammar is difﬁcult. Refer opposite for correct usage.\n                                                                        He weighs 99 kg and is 170cm tall. (verb form)\n                                                                        He weighs 99kg and is 170cm in height. (verb form)\n\n\n\n     Today’s examination revealed multiple missing teeth,               Today’s examination revealed multiple missing teeth,\n     various carious lesions and a periodontal pocket of                various carious lesions and a periodontal pocket\n     depth 4-9mm.                                                       depth of 4-9mm.\n     There are several periodental pockets with about 4-9               There are several periodontal pockets which are about\n     mm in depth.                                                       4’9 mm in depth\n\n     His height was 173cm. Note, weight can change but             or\n     height can not so don’t use past tense.\n                                                                        There are several periodontal pockets with a depth\n Correct word order is:                                                 of about 4-9 mm.\n                                                                        His height is 173cm.\n Depth of 4-9mm\n\n Height of 173cm\n\n Length of 20 m\n\n Weight of 78kg", "extraction": "text", "display": {"version": 2, "text": "Grammar & Vocabular y Clinic\n\nPhysical Decription\n\nReturn to: Topic 5 \n\nCommon Mistakes Regarding Physical Description\n\nIncorrect\n\nCorrect\n\nAdvice was given to reduce her weight.\n\nAdvice was given to reduce weight.\n\nAfter the verb reduce it is not necessary to follow with a\npronoun. So you is not required. Simply say:\n\nThe patient was advised to reduce weight.\n\nA reduction of weight was advised.\n\nI advised him to reduce weight, or, you need to reduce weight.\n\nIn addition, she had lost her weight.\n\nIn addition, she had lost weight.\n\nAfter the verb lose it is not correct to follow with a pronoun.\n\nIn addition, she has lost a further 11 kg of weight over\n\nthe past 2 months.\n\nIn addition, the patient’s weight has signiﬁcantly\n\nreduced from 61 kg to 50 kg over the past 2 months.\n\nHe is now obese with a 99kilos weight and a 170cm height.\n\nHe is now obese with a weight of 99 kg and a height\n\nThe use of the correct verb & noun form and associated\ngrammar is difﬁcult. Refer opposite for correct usage.\n\nof 170cm. (noun form)\n\nHe weighs 99 kg and is 170cm tall. (verb form)\n\nHe weighs 99kg and is 170cm in height. (verb form)\n\nToday’s examination revealed multiple missing teeth,\n\nToday’s examination revealed multiple missing teeth,\n\nvarious carious lesions and a periodontal pocket of\n\nvarious carious lesions and a periodontal pocket\n\ndepth 4-9mm.\n\ndepth of 4-9mm.\n\nThere are several periodental pockets with about 4-9\n\nThere are several periodontal pockets which are about\n\nmm in depth.\n\n4’9 mm in depth\n\nHis height was 173cm. Note, weight can change but\n\nheight can not so don’t use past tense.\n\nCorrect word order is:\n\nDepth of 4-9mm\n\nHeight of 173cm\n\nLength of 20 m\n\nWeight of 78kg\n\nor\n\nThere are several periodontal pockets with a depth\n\nof about 4-9 mm.\n\nHis height is 173cm.", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 612.0, "height": 792.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Grammar & Vocabular y Clinic", "lines": [{"text": "Grammar & Vocabular y Clinic", "x": 0.04092647058823529, "y": 0.06350225252525253, "width": 0.2743826617647059, "height": 0.018493035353535355, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "Grammar", "x": 0.04092647058823529, "width": 0.08648659150326797, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "&", "x": 0.1325017091503268, "width": 0.013395477124183004, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "Vocabular", "x": 0.15098787581699347, "width": 0.09509767810457515, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "y", "x": 0.24825823529411767, "width": 0.010250807189542483, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "Clinic", "x": 0.26360177450980393, "width": 0.05170735784313726, "confidence": 1}]}]}, {"text": "Physical Decription", "lines": [{"text": "Physical Decription", "x": 0.0409264705